  "historical_output_text": " Of cours! Can’t you hear? 😄 Let' say, a frequent problem in the forum that people might face in everyday life.\n\nIf you have trouble getting your sink clogging to unclogging without harmful or pricey chemicals, one method to try out first would not harm any living being, or our environment: Boil two litres water with one tablespoon vinegar (acide, it’s good! ), pour it slowly on to your plugged-up pipe and cover up all of the holes and outlets to avoid water from spitting on. Give a good minute before you add a quarter to an-half of a block/bundle bi-degreasing dishsoap (it should look foamier and a more bubbly after that, it is normal. ). Now let this mix brew up for an half hour to forty minutes.\n\nFinally rinse the drain thoroughly and flush",
